WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.625
Step eight opens the closure register.

2
00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:06.743
Every finding gets one entry
with the closure chain's fields,

3
00:00:06.743 --> 00:00:11.438
from the Zero Trust and Assessment
book: the finding and tool version,

4
00:00:11.438 --> 00:00:15.309
the attack path, the owner,
dependencies, the change, pilot,

5
00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:20.663
enforcement and test, the evidence,
residual risk, reassessment and weighting.

6
00:00:20.663 --> 00:00:23.989
Each finding family routes to
the page that remediates it,

7
00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:26.900
with the evidence that shows
it's ready for closure.

8
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.093
Emergency access goes to
Access and Privilege,

9
00:00:30.093 --> 00:00:32.712
with a test sign-in that fired its alert.

10
00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:36.089
Conditional Access gaps
go to its policy library,

11
00:00:36.089 --> 00:00:38.725
with a test sign-in blocked as designed.

12
00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:41.687
Skipped tests go to step
seven's dispositions.

13
00:00:41.687 --> 00:00:45.525
A finding with no family goes
to the Zero Trust program lead.

14
00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:49.700
The kit sets a default priority,
and the owner writes the rationale.

15
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:53.150
An exception with an expiry
is the see-so's decision;

16
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.025
one without is the authorizing official's.

17
00:00:56.025 --> 00:00:58.940
The kit never marks a
finding ready for closure.
